      <memberdef kind="function" id="_marmot_monomial_basis_functions_8h_1ad5da4f8abb2edab40ace025974aae3b5" prot="public" static="no" const="no" explicit="no" inline="yes" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>int</type>
        <definition>int Marmot::Math::_computeMonomialBasisGradientRecursion</definition>
        <argsstring>(int order, const Eigen::VectorXd &amp;x, Eigen::MatrixXd &amp;res, int idxEnd, int dim)</argsstring>
        <name>_computeMonomialBasisGradientRecursion</name>
        <qualifiedname>Marmot::Math::_computeMonomialBasisGradientRecursion</qualifiedname>
        <param>
          <type>int</type>
          <declname>order</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>const Eigen::VectorXd &amp;</type>
          <declname>x</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>Eigen::MatrixXd &amp;</type>
          <declname>res</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>int</type>
          <declname>idxEnd</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>int</type>
          <declname>dim</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Recursive kernel of computeMonomialBasisGradient(). </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Same traversal as _computeMonomialBasisRecursion(). By the product rule, column <formula id="90">$ k $</formula> of an entry is multiplied by <formula id="91">$ \partial x_k^i / \partial x_k = i\, x_k^{i-1} $</formula> for its own coordinate and by <formula id="92">$ x_j^i $</formula> for all other coordinates <formula id="93">$ j \neq k $</formula>.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">order</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Remaining total degree. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">x</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Coordinates. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="inout">res</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Gradient matrix (basis size <formula id="94">$ \times d $</formula>), initialized with ones by the caller. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">idxEnd</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>First row of <computeroutput>res</computeroutput> treated by this call. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">dim</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Number of (leading) coordinates treated by this call. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>One past the last row of <computeroutput>res</computeroutput> treated by this call. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
